  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 1145 PM CST Tue Nov 10 2026\n\nThursday through Tuesday:\n\nThursday morning, light precip will remain in play from breezy\nnortheast winds and lake effect rain potential. Given cooler \nconditions behind the front with still very warm lake waters, \nsurface to 850mb temperature differences will be around 15-20 \ndegrees. With a period of onshore wind potential some lake \neffect rain showers are possible in southeast WI, primarily\ncloser to the lake but may otherwise remain dry for most of \nsouthern WI. There is some uncertainty on how inland precip gets\nwith certain models suggestive of little to none with other\nbringing precip potential to half the CWA for at least a period. \nThursday night into Friday these conditions will generally \nremain but more northerly winds will keep chances over the lake \nwith high pressure keeping southern WI dry and likely mostly \nclear. However, if we were to manage some lake effect over the \narea Thursday night into Friday a few flakes would be possible.\n\nConditions this weekend continue to look dry as high pressure\nremains overhead and likely even strengthens through the weekend\nand lingers through early next week. \n\nOtherwise cooler weather settles in Thursday night behind the\ndeparted low but will gradually increase through the weekend\ninto next week.\n\nKuroski",
